{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Getting the Client"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Training Ferdinand"}, {"type": "position", "content": 4}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 9}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": " Use expressions about relationships and feelings in a range of social and work contexts. "}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": " Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": " Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": " Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": " Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": " Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": " Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": " Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": " Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn7le09ob04re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Giving Oral Instructions "}, {"type": "describer", "content": " Both in the workplace and in our everyday lives, it is important to ask for instructions as well as be able to give them. The chart below summarizes the most important language you can use. "}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"> <span class=\\\"strong\\\">  Giving Instructions   </span> </div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"> <span class=\\\"strong\\\">   Asking Questions  </span> </div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You can use the following phrases to give instructions: <ul><span class=\\\"italic\\\"> \\t<li>I would like (you) to \u2026 (verb) </li><li>In my experience, the best way to do it is by / to \u2026 </li><li>You need to \u2026 (verb). This is what we call \u2026 I would start by \u2026 (ing) </li><li>It would be helpful to \u2026 (+verb)</li> </ul></span>  You can also use <span class=\\\"strong\\\">imperatives </span>when giving instructions: <ul><span class=\\\"italic\\\"> \\t<li>You are to be responsible for \u2026 </li><li>Be (especially) careful when \u2026 </li><li>Please be sure to \u2026</li> </ul></span>  You should also ask questions when giving instructions: <ul><span class=\\\"italic\\\"> \\t<li>Are you with me? </li> </ul></span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Here are some questions you can ask while you are being given instructions:  <ul><span class=\\\"italic\\\"> \\t<li>Do you mind If I \u2026 (+verb)  </li><li>Could you repeat that?  </li><li>What do you suggest?</li> </ul></span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"> <span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Sequencing </span> </div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"> <span class=\\\"strong\\\">  Responding to Instructions  </span> </div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<ul><span class=\\\"italic\\\"> \\t<li>First (of all) \u2026 </li><li>Next \u2026 </li><li>After that, \u2026 </li><li>Finally \u2026 </li> </ul></span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<ul><span class=\\\"italic\\\"> \\t<li>Go on, I am taking note of everything. </li><li>Please continue. </li><li>Keep going. </li> </ul></span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\"\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"underline\">I would like to</span> go over a list of advice for this specific task. </span> "}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"underline\">Do you mind if I take notes?</span></span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"underline\">First, be</span> aware of your role in this job.</span>. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"underline\">Next</span>, you need to think what software to use.</span> "}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"underline\">Any questions so far?</span></span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"underline\">After that</span>,  you should be able to determine your expenses. </span>"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Intonation in Questions"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " When asking questions in English, it is important to think about your intonation. Intonation is the musical pattern of ups and downs in your voice. It basically describes how the voice rises and falls in speech. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "There are two important intonation patterns in English when asking questions: <br /><br /> <span class=\"strong\">Falling Intonation</span> This describes how your voice falls on the last stressed syllable of a word or group of words. This type of intonation is very common in \"Wh-\" questions. <span class=\"italic\"> <ul> \t<li> How does this relate to my question? </li><li>Where can I stage the next event? \t</li> </ul></span><br /> <span class=\"strong\">Rising Intonation</span> This describes how your voice rises at the end of a sentence. This type of intonation is common in \"yes & no\" questions. <span class=\"italic\"> <ul> \t<li> Do you mind if I take notes? </li><li>Any questions so far? \t</li> </ul></span>"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "crush debt "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to remove money that is owing, quickly and effectively"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  This will help you crush your debt."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le09ob04aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you hear in financial conversations."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "outstanding "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "when referring to debt, the amount of money that remains unpaid"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: This will help you pay off outstanding debt."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le09ob04aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "take charge of "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to assume responsibility for something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Ferdinand will take charge of the company's financial future."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le09ob04aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to track"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " to record the trail, or history of one's activity"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": " (verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You need to start tracking your spending history."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le09ob04aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "estimate"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " an approximate amount"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Put them all together and you will get an estimate of monthly spendings."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le09ob04aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "analytics"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " the systematic computational analysis of data or statistics"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": " (noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You should get a finance software program that has analytics to help project your cash-flow."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le09ob04aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "cash-flow"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " the total amount of money being transferring in and out of a business"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: A software program with analytics can help project your cash-flow."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le09ob04aud07"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "revenue"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "financial  income"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Finally, analyze your revenue and expenses."}, {"ty